 "question": "is there a latent-space map that improves the generated detail? (mapper feasibility)",
 "answer": "no for a latent-target objective, and the experiment shows why in a way that disqualifies the whole class: the latent-domain statistics all IMPROVED while the picture got clearly worse.",
 "step1_decoder_can_emit_detail_only": {
  "result": "yes",
  "file": "results/deploy/null_roundtrip.json",
  "numbers": "round-tripping the true null component n = x - U(Dx) through the frozen VAE returns it at cosine 0.9155, energy ratio 1.023, PSNR 31.93 dB; round-tripping a natural image and taking its null band gives cosine 0.937 / 33.73 dB. Detail-only costs 1.8 dB more than natural, so the decoder output manifold is not the obstacle.",
  "latency_note": "a mapper replaces the input of the decode that already happens, so it adds no decode. An earlier note in this project put the cost at +8.2% for an extra decoder forward; that was wrong -- the decode count is unchanged and only the mapper forward is new."
 },
